1
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:15,317
Far enough away.

2
00:00:15,378 --> 00:00:16,039
Good evening.

3
00:00:16,079 --> 00:00:18,181
I trust you had a fruitful day.

4
00:00:18,321 --> 00:00:21,064
I do not say happy, though I hope it has been happy.

5
00:00:21,103 --> 00:00:37,682
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhodasa Namo Tassa Bhagavato Arahato Sambha Sambhodasa

6
00:00:38,387 --> 00:00:46,475
Namo tassa bhagavato arahato sambha sambuddhasa.

7
00:00:47,055 --> 00:00:51,420
Homage to the Buddha, the blessed noble, and fully self-awakened.

8
00:00:53,881 --> 00:00:57,545
Now then, we're moving on now to another discourse.

9
00:00:59,646 --> 00:01:00,508
And this is number 72.

10
00:01:01,048 --> 00:01:05,153
And we've come across a character called Vachagatha.

11
00:01:05,173 --> 00:01:07,855
He crops up a couple of other times, I think.

12
00:01:08,475 --> 00:01:11,358
And so we'll read it through again and we'll see what this is about.

13
00:01:13,219 --> 00:01:18,125
So on one occasion, the Blessed One was living at Sarvati and Jeta's Grove in Artipindika's Park.

14
00:01:18,144 --> 00:01:19,206
So we've been there before.

15
00:01:19,225 --> 00:01:20,587
It's his favorite place, I think.

16
00:01:22,168 --> 00:01:22,929
And the wanderer.

17
00:01:23,228 --> 00:01:26,371
So he's one of these ascetic wanderers, a Samana.

18
00:01:27,153 --> 00:01:32,137
And often you get people approaching the Buddha as a Samana Gautama.

19
00:01:32,197 --> 00:01:33,718
That's how they would approach him sometimes.

20
00:01:34,799 --> 00:01:38,263
So the wanderer Gautama went to the Blessed One and exchanged greetings with him.

21
00:01:38,816 --> 00:01:46,087
When this courteous and amiable talk was finished, he sat down to one side and asked the Blessed One, How is it, Master Gautama?

22
00:01:46,608 --> 00:01:53,518
Does Master Gautama hold the view, the world is eternal, only this is true, everything else is wrong?

23
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:57,384
Vajagoda, I do not hold this view.

24
00:01:59,066 --> 00:02:06,376
Then does Master Gautama hold the view, the world is not eternal, only this is true, everything else is wrong?

25
00:02:07,066 --> 00:02:10,389
Vachagoda, I do not hold this view.

26
00:02:12,192 --> 00:02:13,493
How is it Master Gautama?

27
00:02:14,294 --> 00:02:17,639
Does Master Gautama hold the view the world is finite?

28
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,604
Is this the only truth and everything else is false?

29
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:25,669
Vachagoda, I do not hold this view.

30
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,814
How then Master Gautama hold the view the world is infinite?

31
00:02:31,716 --> 00:02:34,979
Vacha, I do not hold this view.

32
00:02:35,669 --> 00:02:37,973
How is it, Master Gautama, then?

33
00:02:38,293 --> 00:02:41,298
Is the soul and the body, are they the same?

34
00:02:42,058 --> 00:02:44,282
And is this the only truth, everything else is wrong?

35
00:02:45,082 --> 00:02:47,646
Vacha, I do not hold this view.

36
00:02:49,189 --> 00:02:50,411
How then, Master Gautama?

37
00:02:50,972 --> 00:02:53,575
Is the soul one thing and the body something else?

38
00:02:54,578 --> 00:02:55,639
And only this is true?

39
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:58,282
I do not hold this view, Vacha.

40
00:03:00,306 --> 00:03:01,647
How is it, Master Gautama?

41
00:03:01,669 --> 00:03:03,972
Does Master Gautama hold that after death?

42
00:03:04,237 --> 00:03:08,663
that Tathagata, someone who's fully liberated, exists.

43
00:03:09,084 --> 00:03:09,883
And is this true?

44
00:03:09,924 --> 00:03:10,945
And everything else is false?

45
00:03:12,026 --> 00:03:15,330
Vacha, I do not hold this view.

46
00:03:16,611 --> 00:03:20,376
How then, Master Gautama, after death, does the Tathagata not exist?

47
00:03:21,276 --> 00:03:24,080
Vacha, I do not hold this view.

48
00:03:24,121 --> 00:03:29,026
How is it, Master Gautama, does Master Gautama hold this view?

49
00:03:29,526 --> 00:03:34,211
That after death, the Tathagata both exists and does not exist.

50
00:03:34,663 --> 00:03:37,507
Vacha, I do not hold this view.

51
00:03:37,567 --> 00:03:45,514
How then Master Gautama, after death the Tathagata neither exists nor not exists.

52
00:03:46,555 --> 00:03:49,018
Vacha, I do not hold this view."

53
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:57,806
So by this time Vacha I think has got a little bit upset and he says, how is it then Master Gautama?

54
00:03:58,306 --> 00:04:03,692
When Master Gautama is asked each of these questions,

55
00:04:04,515 --> 00:04:06,359
He replies, I do not hold this view.

56
00:04:08,001 --> 00:04:10,305
What danger does Master Gautama see?

57
00:04:11,205 --> 00:04:15,032
That he does not take up any of these speculative views.

58
00:04:16,754 --> 00:04:32,177
Vacha, the speculative view that the world is eternal is a thicket of views, a wilderness of views, a contortion of views, a vacillation of views, a fetter of views.

59
00:04:33,052 --> 00:04:39,540
It is beset by suffering, by vexation, by despair, and by fever.

60
00:04:40,422 --> 00:04:50,617
And it does not lead to disenchantment, to dispassion, to cessation, to peace, to direct knowledge, to enlightenment, and to nibbana.

61
00:04:53,019 --> 00:04:55,262
That's the opening section.

62
00:04:55,824 --> 00:05:02,333
So now, if we look at these statements, these were obviously something that...

63
00:05:02,701 --> 00:05:05,545
the teachers of that time were arguing about.

64
00:05:06,648 --> 00:05:15,845
And remember that in the full moon, when there's no clouds, it's almost daylight in the tropics.

65
00:05:16,386 --> 00:05:20,031
And they would go to the local shrine, which was like a park.

66
00:05:20,754 --> 00:05:21,654
It was very beautiful.

67
00:05:21,714 --> 00:05:24,220
The scriptures say these were very beautiful places.

68
00:05:24,622 --> 00:05:28,166
And they would sit there and listen to these different teachers.

69
00:05:28,848 --> 00:05:31,031
And often there'd be debates, one against the other.

70
00:05:31,653 --> 00:05:34,396
And one would be defeated and humiliated.

71
00:05:34,416 --> 00:05:37,000
The other one would be very conceited and proud.

72
00:05:39,064 --> 00:05:43,389
So these were the, as we say, regular questions, it seems.

73
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:47,105
So it's about the world being eternal and not eternal.

74
00:05:48,105 --> 00:05:50,288
I don't know what we understand these days.

75
00:05:50,309 --> 00:05:54,132
They say the universe is continuously expanding.

76
00:05:54,233 --> 00:05:55,634
So I don't know where that's going to take us.

77
00:05:58,678 --> 00:06:00,540
So the world is eternal or not eternal.

78
00:06:00,781 --> 00:06:04,406
And then the one was about the world is finite or is it infinite?

79
00:06:05,307 --> 00:06:06,528
So that's to do with space.

80
00:06:06,567 --> 00:06:10,372
The first one is to do with time and the second one to do with space.

81
00:06:11,146 --> 00:06:15,992
And then the third one, the third trilogy was the body and the soul.

82
00:06:16,733 --> 00:06:22,742
So some people thought the body and the soul were the same, so they would have been the materialists, when you die, you die.

83
00:06:23,142 --> 00:06:28,750
But others thought or held the view that the soul and the body were different, and the soul went to heaven.

84
00:06:30,091 --> 00:06:35,819
Now the soul here stands for the heart-mind, what we would call heart-mind.

85
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:47,869
the chitta, though they use various words, but the five khandhas, if you remember the five khandhas, this also comes up in this discourse.

86
00:06:48,355 --> 00:06:51,057
So the body, and then you have the mind.

87
00:06:51,117 --> 00:06:53,540
So the body, mind, heart, mind.

88
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:57,464
So one is all the feelings, all the perceptions and concepts.

89
00:06:57,805 --> 00:07:00,709
Then you've got all your habits of thought, et cetera, et cetera.

90
00:07:01,088 --> 00:07:04,392
And of course, consciousness, the screen upon which it all arises.

91
00:07:04,894 --> 00:07:11,961
So was this body separate from the rest or was the rest the same?

92
00:07:12,601 --> 00:07:15,966
So it was obviously a core question in terms of rebirth.

93
00:07:16,687 --> 00:07:25,201
Because it's that which takes, it's the mind, heart, mind or the soul, which, of course, keeps taking rebirth.

94
00:07:28,947 --> 00:07:31,891
So that was the next duo.

95
00:07:32,793 --> 00:07:35,958
And then there's these questions which were known as the quadrilemma.

96
00:07:36,338 --> 00:07:39,182
And the first one, of course, is pretty straightforward.

97
00:07:40,024 --> 00:07:44,771
Does somebody who's fully liberated exist in some way after death?

98
00:07:45,410 --> 00:07:47,552
Or does he not exist, right?

99
00:07:47,692 --> 00:07:49,535
Does he completely disappear or something?

100
00:07:50,716 --> 00:07:54,240
Is it also some form of annihilation?

101
00:07:54,262 --> 00:07:58,947
In a sense, there can only be one form of annihilation, but basically, does he no longer exist?

102
00:07:59,588 --> 00:08:11,423
And then there's this, when they try to get it both together, exist and not exist, trying to get it, so there's this mixture of being existing and yet not existing.

103
00:08:11,644 --> 00:08:13,846
So these are logical propositions.

104
00:08:14,113 --> 00:08:16,956
which really don't make much sense.

105
00:08:17,096 --> 00:08:22,322
And the last one is neither exists nor not exists.

106
00:08:22,343 --> 00:08:28,129
So again, neither exists nor not exists, then that sounds very much like nothing at all.

107
00:08:28,189 --> 00:08:30,230
That's beyond nothing at all.

108
00:08:32,313 --> 00:08:43,985
I read one writer, I can't remember now the book I read it in, but he thought that the Buddha should have said yes to that because it's a complete denial of everything.

109
00:08:44,370 --> 00:08:51,941
But the Buddha wasn't into taking any position speculative, any metaphysical position as such.

110
00:08:53,121 --> 00:08:57,548
So Vajragocha is a little bit upset with him.

111
00:08:57,587 --> 00:08:58,448
He says everything is wrong.

112
00:08:58,850 --> 00:09:02,855
And the Buddha says he doesn't take to speculative views.

113
00:09:03,755 --> 00:09:06,921
And part of speculative views are inferences.

114
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:10,345
So there's no teaching beyond inferences.

115
00:09:10,966 --> 00:09:16,013
the individual experience of Nibbāna, of that liberation.

116
00:09:16,634 --> 00:09:30,131
There's no teaching concerning what is my Nibbāna in relation to your Nibbāna, and do we all belong to one big Nibbāna, etc.

117
00:09:30,493 --> 00:09:34,217
So anything that's inferred, the Buddha just wouldn't go there.

118
00:09:34,238 --> 00:09:38,003
He was basically rooted in what we could experience.

119
00:09:38,523 --> 00:09:55,791
And the main experience was this liberation from suffering and this complete freedom from any attachment, this craving, this seeking of any real happiness, proper happiness in the world.

120
00:09:57,234 --> 00:10:00,379
And that's what he's, his whole teaching is based on that.

121
00:10:00,982 --> 00:10:14,333
he actually said he only taught suffering or dukkha, which remember it includes also attachment to pleasant things, and the end of it, you know, and the Four Noble Truths, that's what it's about, isn't it?

122
00:10:14,413 --> 00:10:28,725
It's the basic statement of what constitutes unhappiness for us, suffering and discomfort and all that, and what causes it, there is an end to it and the path leading to the end of it.

123
00:10:29,187 --> 00:10:30,567
So he's very rooted in

124
00:10:31,038 --> 00:10:59,424
in direct experience and he doesn't want to go beyond that into this speculative view business so um and then then he goes through all those propositions that thatcher gota has given him concerning all these speculative views um then uh he's asked uh does master gotama hold any speculative view at all

125
00:11:00,046 --> 00:11:04,855
So Vacha, speculative view, is something that the Tathagata has put away.

126
00:11:05,937 --> 00:11:09,322
For the Tathagata Vacha has seen this now.

127
00:11:09,943 --> 00:11:14,812
Such is material form, such its origin, such its disappearance.

128
00:11:15,394 --> 00:11:19,000
Such is feeling, such its origin and its disappearance.

129
00:11:19,434 --> 00:11:31,610
such is perception, such is origin and disappearance, such are habits, formation, volitional formations, their origin and their disappearance, and consciousness, their origin and disappearance."

130
00:11:31,629 --> 00:11:45,307
In other words, what the Buddha has truly understood are these five aggregates that we experience as our selves, the psycho-physical organism.

131
00:11:45,447 --> 00:11:47,669
He's understood it thoroughly.

132
00:11:48,679 --> 00:12:15,952
Therefore I say that the destruction, fading away, cessation, giving up and relinquishing of all conceivings, all conceptual thinking, all excogitations, which is basically thinking something through, all eye-making, all mind-making, this is me, this is mine, and the underlying tendency to conceit,

133
00:12:16,287 --> 00:12:42,143
that the targeter is liberated through not clinging so uh when these three things come together you then form uh should we say a position a view an opinion where you where you you sort of uh take a position if i'm right and everybody else is wrong it takes a view right you have a view about something

134
00:12:42,409 --> 00:12:49,077
you have an attachment to that view because you identify with it.

135
00:12:49,438 --> 00:12:50,860
This is what I think.

136
00:12:50,900 --> 00:12:52,423
This is what I believe.

137
00:12:52,903 --> 00:12:55,986
And you can see that very clearly when it comes to politics.

138
00:12:57,990 --> 00:13:04,136
And when it comes to fundamentalists, you see that then it comes in sharp relief.

139
00:13:04,638 --> 00:13:07,741
You know, I'm right and everybody else is wrong.

140
00:13:12,211 --> 00:13:20,761
So then the Buddha goes on to say, when a bhikkhu's mind is liberated thus, where does he appear after death?

141
00:13:21,283 --> 00:13:24,125
Now, I'm going to stop there.

142
00:13:24,145 --> 00:13:25,648
It's a little bit early, I know.

143
00:13:26,149 --> 00:13:36,402
It's short on the old discourse because the next part moves on to a slightly different topic.

144
00:13:36,422 --> 00:13:40,226
So just to recap there, you'll come across these ten

145
00:13:40,527 --> 00:13:47,634
um views about the the world being finite or infinite eternal or non-eternal

146
00:13:47,985 --> 00:13:54,153
You'll come across the idea about the soul and the body being one or not the same.

147
00:13:54,475 --> 00:13:59,782
And this quadrilemma, not a dilemma, this quadrilemma that they talk about the Buddha.

148
00:14:00,241 --> 00:14:10,936
And the important thing about this is that the Buddha won't hold on to any speculative views, any views beyond what you can directly experience.

149
00:14:12,619 --> 00:14:15,883
And he doesn't go on to anything beyond that.

150
00:14:16,116 --> 00:14:35,812
And so any inference, anything that you infer, so if you infer, for instance, that, well, there must be some sort of huge intelligence, sort of an awareness, an intuitive awareness of which we are all part.

151
00:14:36,485 --> 00:14:44,317
You know, that might be a sort of panentheism, God is everywhere or some such idea.

152
00:14:44,758 --> 00:14:46,059
See, he wouldn't go there at all.

153
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:53,471
He would consider that to be an inference, an inference, a speculative view and not material.

154
00:14:53,532 --> 00:14:54,113
This is the point.

155
00:14:54,533 --> 00:14:56,956
It's not material to personal liberation.

156
00:14:57,341 --> 00:14:59,986
So there were two reasons why he wouldn't go there.

157
00:15:00,067 --> 00:15:03,072
First of all, there was no way you could prove it, right?

158
00:15:03,734 --> 00:15:09,725
And secondly, it had no direct effect upon this whole process of liberating ourselves from suffering.

159
00:15:10,787 --> 00:15:16,297
So this is Vachagota, and we'll finish off the discourse tomorrow evening.

160
00:15:16,999 --> 00:15:19,923
So I hope that...

161
00:15:20,883 --> 00:15:50,501
this has not caused any confusion but in fact has been a most enlightening discourse uh to to go through and i trust that by your continuing practice you will be liberated as that you go to was uh from all suffering sooner rather than later so we can do a bit of meditation

